# Bootstrap demotion specification
#
# The historical tape files each contain two Cambridge SECTIONs separated by
# a standalone '.' end-of-section marker. Do not apply this as a simple
# in-place patch to source/syn or source/trn. The bootstrap derivative is a
# four-file split that preserves those section boundaries.
#
# Historical source mapping:
#
#   source/syn:
#       SECTION "SYN"  ...  .  SECTION "LEX"  ...
#         -> demoted/syn
#         -> demoted/lex
#
#   source/trn:
#       SECTION "TRNA" ...  .  SECTION "TRNB" ...
#         -> demoted/trna
#         -> demoted/trnb
#
# Transformations allowed in the first derivative:
#
#   1. Remove the SECTION "..." wrapper at the start of each split unit.
#   2. Remove the standalone '.' separator because the units are physically
#      separate files after splitting.
#   3. Rewrite source-level '~=' as the MR10-supported 'NE' spelling.
#   4. Make no other source, header, runtime, driver, or semantic changes.
#
# Known ~= occurrences established so far:
#
#   SYN:
#       GETBYTE(SECTIONNAME, 0) ~= 0
#     becomes
#       GETBYTE(SECTIONNAME, 0) NE 0
#
#   TRNA:
#       GETBYTE(SECTIONNAME, 0) ~= 0
#     becomes
#       GETBYTE(SECTIONNAME, 0) NE 0
#
# This file is intentionally a specification rather than an automatically
# applicable unified diff: the essential first operation is splitting two
# historical container files into four bootstrap compilation units.
